{% extends "commons/base.njk" %}
{% import "partials/access.njk" as login with context %}

{#
  The pre-analysis page: the rounds of questions, one message at a time, with the
  summary of what was settled when the request set off next to them.

  The conversation and the turns live on the open step of the project's pipeline,
  the credit on the user's record, and reloading the page loses nothing.

  **The preanalyst speaks first.** There is no opening message written here: whoever
  arrives has just answered a form and has nothing to say yet, so with an empty
  conversation the browser asks `POST /preanalysis/{id}/opening` and the first
  real question comes back from the preanalyst. It is written onto the step like any
  other message, which is why the loop below prints it on a reload without anything
  special.

  The turns — a question and its answer — are counted by the server. When
  `chat.warn_when_left` are left the warning appears; at zero the field for writing
  is hidden and the out-of-turns box takes its place, from which turns can be added
  out of the credit. If the turns come back, the field comes back.

  The markup of a message lives in the two <template>s at the bottom, not inside
  `public/preanalysis.js`: composing HTML from strings in the JavaScript would make
  escaping a matter of memory, and here the text is written by the user. The
  browser clones the model and fills `.chat-text` with `textContent`, which gives
  birth to no HTML. For the same reason the turns warning and the out-of-turns box
  are already here, switched off: the JavaScript switches them on and writes no
  text.

  Without JavaScript the page stays readable — heading, the conversation as it
  stands, field, summary — but nothing is sent, and on a conversation that has not
  begun there is nothing to read yet: the first question is asked by the browser.
#}

{% block header_extra %}
      <div class="header-access">
      {{- login.header(access) }}
      </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="container chat">
      <div class="chat-intro reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.eyebrow") }}</div>
        <h1>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.heading") }}</h1>
        <p class="chat-lead">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.lead") }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="chat-layout">
        {#- Where to write and what is left: the browser has neither the catalogues
            nor the configuration, and gets the numbers it needs from the page. #}
        <div class="chat-panel card reveal delay-1"
             data-chat-project="{{ chat.project_id }}"
             data-chat-turns-left="{{ chat.turns_left }}"
             data-chat-warn-left="{{ chat.warn_when_left }}"
             data-chat-credit="{{ chat.credit }}"
             data-chat-closed="{{ "true" if chat.closed else "false" }}">
          {#- `aria-live`: a message that arrives on its own must be announced, or
              whoever is not looking at the screen does not know it came. #}
          <ol class="chat-log" data-chat-log aria-live="polite">
{%- for message in chat.messages %}
            <li class="chat-turn chat-turn-{{ "client" if message.role == "client" else "system" }}">
              <div class="chat-who">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.you") if message.role == "client" else t("preanalyst.preanalysis.system") }}</div>
              <div class="chat-bubble"><p class="chat-text">{{ message.text }}</p></div>
            </li>
{%- endfor %}
          </ol>

          {#- The pre-analysis has been judged complete: the preanalyst proposed to
              close and `src/preanalysis_validator.js` agreed. It is a notice, not the end
              of anything — whoever has turns left goes on writing if there is
              something to add, and the verdict is that of the last turn, so it
              goes away again if a later turn reopens the questions.

              `hidden` is decided by the server: the verdict lives on the step, and
              a page reloaded after it must open with the notice already there. #}
          <p class="chat-ready" data-chat-ready{% if not chat.ready %} hidden{% endif %}>
            {{- t("preanalyst.preanalysis.ready") }}
          </p>

          {#- The rounds are over: this page is a reading of the conversation. It is
              decided by the server and the browser never changes it, so it is
              written or it is not — there is no `hidden` to toggle. #}
{%- if chat.closed %}
          <p class="chat-closed">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.closed") }}</p>
{%- endif %}

          <p class="chat-waiting" data-chat-waiting hidden>
            <span class="chat-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.waiting") }}</span>
          </p>

          {#- One message at a time: until the answer has arrived the field and the
              button stay disabled. Once the turns are gone it all disappears.

              `hidden` is written here and not left to the JavaScript: a page that
              opens with the turns already gone must not show, even for an instant,
              a field that cannot be used. #}
          <form class="chat-composer" data-chat-form{% if chat.closed or chat.turns_left <= 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
            {#- No `maxlength`: the browser would cut what is pasted into it, in
                silence and where the server never sees it, which is the thing this
                field stopped doing. Too long is answered, not prevented. #}
            <textarea class="input chat-input" id="chat-message" name="message" rows="2"
                      aria-label="{{ t('preanalyst.preanalysis.label') }}"
                      placeholder="{{ t('preanalyst.preanalysis.placeholder') }}"
                      data-chat-input></textarea>
            <div class="chat-actions">
              <p class="chat-hint">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.hint") }}</p>
              <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit" data-chat-send>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.send") }}</button>
            </div>
            {#- Switched on from `warn_from_turn` onwards. Small: it is information,
                not an alarm, and somebody who is writing must not be interrupted.
                It says what happens when they run out, because the number alone
                would not.

                The number comes before the noun ("available: 1 of 5") and not
                after: that way the sentence does not change between one and more
                than one, and the JavaScript writes a number instead of choosing a
                form. #}
            <p class="chat-turns-warning" data-chat-warning hidden>
              {{- t_html("preanalyst.preanalysis.turns.warning", { left: chat.turns_left, max: chat.total }) }}
            </p>
            {#- When the call does not succeed. This text too lives in the catalogue
                and in the page: the JavaScript only switches it on. #}
            <p class="chat-error" data-chat-error hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.error") }}</p>
            {#- Its own line, because its own reason: the turn did not happen, and
                what has to be done about it is not "try again" but "make it
                shorter". The number comes from the configuration. #}
            <p class="chat-error" data-chat-error-too-long hidden>
              {{- t("preanalyst.preanalysis.too_long", { limit: chat.max_chars }) }}
            </p>
          </form>

          {#- It takes the field's place when the turns are gone. If the turns then
              come back — from the credit or from a purchase — this is switched off
              and the field reappears: it is not an end, it is an interruption.

              With credit, the field for moving some onto the project is shown and
              the purchase is hidden; without credit the field is disabled and the
              purchase is shown. The two never appear together. #}
          <div class="chat-exhausted" data-chat-exhausted{% if chat.closed or chat.turns_left > 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
            <h2 class="chat-exhausted-title">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.title") }}</h2>
            <p class="chat-exhausted-lead">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.lead", { max: chat.total }) }}</p>

            <div class="chat-credit">
              <p class="chat-credit-line" data-chat-credit-line>
                {{- t_html("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.credit_available", { credit: chat.credit }) }}
              </p>
              <p class="chat-credit-line" data-chat-credit-empty hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.credit_none") }}</p>
              {#- The purchase sits on the same line as the adding, when the line
                  has room for it: it is the other way of getting turns, not
                  another subject. Without room it goes below on its own, because
                  the row wraps. #}
              <div class="chat-credit-row">
                <label class="chat-credit-label" for="chat-turns">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.credit_label") }}</label>
                <input class="input chat-credit-input" type="number" id="chat-turns" name="turns"
                       min="1" step="1" value="1" data-chat-turns-input>
                <button class="btn" type="button" data-chat-use-credit>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.use_credit") }}</button>
                <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-chat-buy hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.buy") }}</button>
              </div>
              {#- What is wrong with the number written, said while it is being
                  written and not when the button is pressed: a button that answers
                  nothing looks broken. Two sentences and not one, because asking
                  for fewer turns and asking for a number at all are two different
                  mistakes. Only one is ever on. #}
              <p class="chat-error" data-chat-turns-too-many hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.credit_too_many") }}</p>
              <p class="chat-error" data-chat-turns-invalid hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.credit_invalid") }}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="chat-exhausted-hint">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.optional") }}</p>
            <p class="chat-exhausted-hint">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.exhausted.download_hint") }}</p>
            <p class="chat-error" data-chat-exhausted-error hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.error") }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        {#- The summary. It is read and not touched: these terms were settled when
            the request set off and are not changed here. #}
        <aside class="chat-aside card reveal delay-2" aria-labelledby="chat-summary-title">
          <div class="card-head aside-head" id="chat-summary-title">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.title") }}</div>
          <div class="chat-aside-body">
{%- if summary.empty %}
            <p class="chat-summary-empty">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.empty") }}</p>
{%- else %}
            <dl class="chat-summary">
{%- if summary.driver %}
              <dt>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.driver") }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ summary.driver.name }}</dd>
{%- endif %}
{%- if summary.discount %}
              <dt>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.discount") }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.discount_value", { percentage: summary.discount.percentage }) }}</dd>
{%- endif %}
{%- if summary.ambassador %}
              <dt>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.ambassador") }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ summary.ambassador.name }}</dd>
{%- endif %}
{%- if summary.autonomous %}
              <dt>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.autonomous") }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.autonomous_value") }}</dd>
{%- endif %}
            </dl>
{%- endif %}

            <dl class="chat-summary chat-summary-turns">
              <dt>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.turns.label") }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ t_html("preanalyst.preanalysis.turns.value", { used: chat.used, max: chat.total }) }}</dd>
            </dl>

            {#- The go button is born `disabled` and stays so without JavaScript:
                what it does lives there. `public/preanalysis.js` switches it on
                when the pre-analysis has been judged complete, or when the turns
                have run out — the two roads out of the conversation. #}
            <div class="chat-aside-actions">
              <button class="btn" type="button" data-chat-download>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.download") }}</button>
              <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-chat-go disabled>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.go") }}</button>
              {#- Shown once the analysis has been asked for. It says that and no
                  more: no page shows the analysis yet, and nothing tells anybody
                  when it is ready. #}
              <p class="chat-ready" data-chat-started hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.summary.started") }}</p>
              <p class="chat-error" data-chat-go-error hidden>{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.error") }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      {#- The models of the two messages. The browser clones them and fills in the
          text only: the name of who is speaking is already written here, in the
          right language. #}
      <template data-chat-template="client">
        <li class="chat-turn chat-turn-client">
          <div class="chat-who">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.you") }}</div>
          <div class="chat-bubble"><p class="chat-text"></p></div>
        </li>
      </template>
      <template data-chat-template="system">
        <li class="chat-turn chat-turn-system">
          <div class="chat-who">{{ t("preanalyst.preanalysis.system") }}</div>
          <div class="chat-bubble"><p class="chat-text"></p></div>
        </li>
      </template>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script src="/preanalysis.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
